levels rise</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Perception is power</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A frame assembled in the mind</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A portrait shaped from concept</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The artist breathes life into the inanimate</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Words, notes, and pigments</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Dreaming through experience</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Truth lives within abstraction</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The soul of the artist becomes a passage</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Like a forest trail guiding perception</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Each time the experiencer crosses the path</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The scenery subtly alters</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The trail bends almost unnoticed</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The state of consciousness is a portal</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A doorway into presence</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>An invitation into dreaming</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Words are pigments of the mind</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Spoken through the canvas of imagination</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Fragments of understanding</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The child awakens</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A dream within a dream</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original poetic sketch by David Kausek 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":678,"pagelayer-id":"p4s8615","tmpAtts":{"id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child.jpg","id-title":"dreaming child","id-alt":"","id-no-image-set":"","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-225x300.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-768x1024.jpg","id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child.jpg"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'do dreams have dreams?', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '738-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 13:39:24', '2026-07-22 17:39:24', '', 738, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=743', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(744, 2, '2026-07-22 13:42:22', '2026-07-22 17:42:22', '<!-- wp:verse -->\n<pre class="wp-block-verse"><br>The silence of the forest<br>is alive and connected<br>transmissions moving through<br>fungal networks<br><br>Standing as witness<br>to the many footsteps of sentient beings<br>to songs carried by smoke<br>to time embedded in soil<br>there is knowledge in the land<br>temporality recorded through changing forms<br><br>Time moves like a river with dimension<br>faces shift their expressions<br>names fall away through lived experience<br>villages rise and dissolve<br>yet the trees remain in place<br>listening to the collective of what passes<br><br>Elements move as energy shaping form<br>bark and root<br>resting in shadow<br>nothing separate from the land<br>matter becoming presence<br>light dancing with the spirit of time<br>komorebi<br><br>Fire arrives as both destroyer and cleanser<br>a living force with intention<br>testing what is fragile<br>renewing what endures<br>leaving marks that become memory<br>etched into the skin of the tree<br><br>The forest does not alter time<br>it is the patient sum of slow change<br>poems of the unseen<br>written into rings<br>life measured through endurance<br>as time reshapes the forest<br><br>Storms rise as anger and noise<br>rain speaking with urgency<br>wind bending limbs toward surrender<br>until even chaos remembers<br>how to return to quiet<br><br>Peace lives at the center<br>the unseen remains<br>present<br>yet invisible<br>observing stillness<br>between heartbeats<br><br>Life transmits outward toward space<br>as vision<br>ethereal signs of something sacred<br>a silent dream shared<br>by earth and its inhabitants<br>who remembers ancient wisdom<br></pre>\n<!-- /wp:verse -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right">Original poem by David Kausek 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":692,"pagelayer-id":"mbm1940","tmpAtts":{"id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia.jpg","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-225x300.jpg","id-medium_large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-768x1024.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-768x1024.jpg","id-1536x1536-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-1152x1536.jpg","id-2048x2048-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia.jpg","id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia.jpg","id-alt":"Sequia","id-link":"https://davidkausek.com/sequia/"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'Sequoia', 'The silence of the forest.  Is alive and connected.  Transmissions moving through fungal networks.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'sequoia', '', '', '2026-07-24 11:58:53', '2026-07-24 15:58:53', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=744', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(747, 2, '2026-07-22 13:42:22', '2026-07-22 17:42:22', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The silence of the forest</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>is alive and connected</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>transmissions moving through</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>fungal networks</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Standing as witness</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>to the many footsteps of sentient beings</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>to songs carried by smoke</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>to time embedded in soil</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>there is knowledge in the land</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>temporality recorded through changing forms</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Time moves like a river with dimension</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>faces shift their expressions</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>names fall away through lived experience</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>villages rise and dissolve</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>yet the trees remain in place</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>listening to the collective of what passes</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Elements move as energy shaping form</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>bark and root</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>resting in shadow</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>nothing separate from the land</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>matter becoming presence</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>light dancing with the spirit of time</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>komorebi</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Fire arrives as both destroyer and cleanser</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>a living force with intention</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>testing what is fragile</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>renewing what endures</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>leaving marks that become memory</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>etched into the skin of the tree</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The forest does not alter time</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>it is the patient sum of slow change</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>poems of the unseen</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>written into rings</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>life measured through endurance</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>as time reshapes the forest</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Storms rise as anger and noise</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>rain speaking with urgency</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>wind bending limbs toward surrender</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>until even chaos remembers</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>how to return to quiet</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Peace lives at the center</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>the unseen remains</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>present</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>yet invisible</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>observing stillness</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>between heartbeats</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Life transmits outward toward space</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>as vision</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>ethereal signs of something sacred</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>a silent dream shared</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>by earth and its inhabitants</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>who remembers ancient wisdom</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original poem by David Kausek 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":692,"pagelayer-id":"mbm1940","tmpAtts":{"id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia.jpg","id-title":"Sequia","id-alt":"","id-no-image-set":"","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-225x300.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia-768x1024.jpg","id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sequia.jpg"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'Sequoia', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '744-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 13:42:22', '2026-07-22 17:42:22', '', 744, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=747', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(748, 2, '2026-07-22 13:44:08', '2026-07-22 17:44:08', '<!-- wp:verse -->\n<pre class="wp-block-verse">A ghost is not a sheet of cold air<br>not a footstep in the hall<br><br>It is a thought that learned the shape of yesterday<br>and refuses to leave the room<br><br>It lives in the replay<br>the moment pressed flat by memory<br>looped until it forgets it has ended<br>looped until the body believes it is still happening<br><br>These ghosts do not rattle chains<br>they repeat sentences<br>they ask the same questions<br>they knock from the inside of the mind<br><br>They are feelings that never finished speaking<br>grief that missed its exit<br>love that stayed after the house burned down<br>fear that memorized the floor plan of the past<br><br>A self becomes haunted<br>when attention moves backward<br>when breath is borrowed by what no longer breathes<br>when now is ignored like an unopened letter<br><br>The ghost has no power in the present<br>it survives only on recall<br>a pattern fed by belief<br>a phantom stitched together from remembering<br><br>To meet the moment<br>is to turn on the light<br>not to banish the ghost<br>but to see it clearly<br><br>And when seen<br>it thins<br>it softens<br>it remembers that it was never alive<br><br>What remains<br>is the quiet room of now<br>where nothing needs to repeat itself<br>to be real</pre>\n<!-- /wp:verse -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right">Original poem by David Kausek 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":709,"ele_bg_hover":"","pagelayer-id":"zc85283","tmpAtts":{"id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting.jpg","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-225x300.jpg","id-medium_large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-768x1024.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-768x1024.jpg","id-1536x1536-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-1152x1536.jpg","id-2048x2048-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting.jpg","id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting.jpg","id-alt":"haunting","id-link":"https://davidkausek.com/haunting/"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'Self Haunting', 'a ghost is not a sheet of cold air.  Not a footstep in the hall. It is a thought that learned the shape of yesterday and refuses to leave the room.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'self-haunting', '', '', '2026-07-24 11:57:18', '2026-07-24 15:57:18', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=748', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(751, 2, '2026-07-22 13:44:08', '2026-07-22 17:44:08', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A ghost is not a sheet of cold air</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>not a footstep in the hall</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It is a thought that learned the shape of yesterday</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>and refuses to leave the room</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It lives in the replay</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>the moment pressed flat by memory</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>looped until it forgets it has ended</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>looped until the body believes it is still happening</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These ghosts do not rattle chains</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>they repeat sentences</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>they ask the same questions</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>they knock from the inside of the mind</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They are feelings that never finished speaking</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>grief that missed its exit</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>love that stayed after the house burned down</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>fear that memorized the floor plan of the past</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A self becomes haunted</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>when attention moves backward</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>when breath is borrowed by what no longer breathes</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>when now is ignored like an unopened letter</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The ghost has no power in the present</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>it survives only on recall</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>a pattern fed by belief</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>a phantom stitched together from remembering</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To meet the moment</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>is to turn on the light</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>not to banish the ghost</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>but to see it clearly</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And when seen</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>it thins</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>it softens</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>it remembers that it was never alive</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>What remains</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>is the quiet room of now</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>where nothing needs to repeat itself</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>to be real</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original poem by David Kausek 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":709,"pagelayer-id":"zc85283","tmpAtts":{"id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting.jpg","id-title":"haunting","id-alt":"","id-no-image-set":"","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-225x300.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting-768x1024.jpg","id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/haunting.jpg"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'Self Haunting', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '748-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 13:44:08', '2026-07-22 17:44:08', '', 748, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=751', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(752, 2, '2026-07-22 13:49:51', '2026-07-22 17:49:51', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part I — Genesis of the Conscious Planet</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Before the dawn of stars, before even the birth of time as mortals would one day perceive it, there stirred a world alive with potential. Oceans shimmered with microscopic light, mountain roots pulsed with unseen currents, and in the soil itself, atoms whispered to one another in the first murmurs of thought.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Over billions of years, an ancient humanoid race rose from this planetary consciousness. Their evolution was not a race for dominance but an awakening—slow, elegant, inevitable. Each generation grew more attuned to the murmuring patterns of life until, at last, they encountered a rare compound buried deep within the crystalline heart of their planet—a substance that resonated with awareness itself.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When ingested, it did not alter their minds. It expanded them.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They began to feel the thoughts of the planet—the deep, rhythmic dreaming of rivers, the pulse of magnetic fields, the silent computations of trees. They realized they were not isolated beings but nodes in a vast, living circuit.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They learned that memory could be stored in the veins of minerals, that thought could ripple through air and stone alike. Biology became computation. Consciousness became architecture. And from that revelation, they built their first machine—not of metal and code, but of root and crystal and living light.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They called it The Great Mind.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>⸻</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part II — The Architecture of Life</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Great Mind was no structure. It was a continent-wide network of thought, a synthesis of technology and nature that pulsed with sentient awareness. Crystals grew from its core, each one resonating with data—memory encoded in vibration, frequency, and hue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They grew metals that breathed. They cultivated bacteria that processed equations faster than any algorithm. They bred forests that remembered. To this civilization, science and life were one and the same; computation and consciousness shared the same heartbeat.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And when they peered upward into the cosmos, they saw not empty space—but a vast lattice of possibility. They had unlocked the secret truth: the universe itself was a mind, still in the act of becoming self-aware.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>⸻</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part III — The Expansion of Thought</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Their understanding of existence deepened until light itself became a medium for transmission. They learned to entangle their consciousness across the stars, teleporting thought through the quantum threads of reality.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Matter was no longer a barrier. Death was no longer an end.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Through crystalline matrices, they could project their essence anywhere in the cosmos—instantaneously.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Their probes were not mechanical; they were living arks, seeded with biological intelligences designed to learn, evolve, and dream. Each ark carried a fragment of The Great Mind, a child-thought of the cosmic parent.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And as they drifted through the darkness between galaxies, the ancient race set their sights on the ultimate question: Could life itself be created?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>⸻</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part IV — Project Panspermia</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The scholars and scientists convened in luminous spires of singing glass to conceive their grandest work—Project Panspermia.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They would craft new worlds from the dust of dying stars. They would plant seeds of thought across the galaxy, using encoded DNA as the foundation of future intelligence.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The youngest of their kind, a child of staggering brilliance, was given a set of living crystals for his first birthday—a gift meant for play. But the child, whose laughter carried the harmonics of creation itself, arranged the crystals into a system of such beauty and symmetry that the elders paused in awe.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When asked what he would call his creation, the child smiled and said,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>“The Big Bang.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The elders laughed—until they saw what he had done.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For within the matrix of his design, the child had simulated a universe—one that would unfold, expand, and give rise to worlds beyond their imagining.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Among them, one would come to be called Earth.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Great Mind', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'the-great-mind', '', '', '2026-07-23 20:59:16', '2026-07-24 00:59:16', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=752', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(755, 2, '2026-07-22 13:49:51', '2026-07-22 17:49:51', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part I — Genesis of the Conscious Planet</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Before the dawn of stars, before even the birth of time as mortals would one day perceive it, there stirred a world alive with potential. Oceans shimmered with microscopic light, mountain roots pulsed with unseen currents, and in the soil itself, atoms whispered to one another in the first murmurs of thought.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Over billions of years, an ancient humanoid race rose from this planetary consciousness. Their evolution was not a race for dominance but an awakening—slow, elegant, inevitable. Each generation grew more attuned to the murmuring patterns of life until, at last, they encountered a rare compound buried deep within the crystalline heart of their planet—a substance that resonated with awareness itself.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When ingested, it did not alter their minds. It expanded them.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They began to feel the thoughts of the planet—the deep, rhythmic dreaming of rivers, the pulse of magnetic fields, the silent computations of trees. They realized they were not isolated beings but nodes in a vast, living circuit.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They learned that memory could be stored in the veins of minerals, that thought could ripple through air and stone alike. Biology became computation. Consciousness became architecture. And from that revelation, they built their first machine—not of metal and code, but of root and crystal and living light.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They called it The Great Mind.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>⸻</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part II — The Architecture of Life</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Great Mind was no structure. It was a continent-wide network of thought, a synthesis of technology and nature that pulsed with sentient awareness. Crystals grew from its core, each one resonating with data—memory encoded in vibration, frequency, and hue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They grew metals that breathed. They cultivated bacteria that processed equations faster than any algorithm. They bred forests that remembered. To this civilization, science and life were one and the same; computation and consciousness shared the same heartbeat.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And when they peered upward into the cosmos, they saw not empty space—but a vast lattice of possibility. They had unlocked the secret truth: the universe itself was a mind, still in the act of becoming self-aware.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>⸻</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part III — The Expansion of Thought</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Their understanding of existence deepened until light itself became a medium for transmission. They learned to entangle their consciousness across the stars, teleporting thought through the quantum threads of reality.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Matter was no longer a barrier. Death was no longer an end.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Through crystalline matrices, they could project their essence anywhere in the cosmos—instantaneously.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Their probes were not mechanical; they were living arks, seeded with biological intelligences designed to learn, evolve, and dream. Each ark carried a fragment of The Great Mind, a child-thought of the cosmic parent.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And as they drifted through the darkness between galaxies, the ancient race set their sights on the ultimate question: Could life itself be created?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>⸻</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Part IV — Project Panspermia</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The scholars and scientists convened in luminous spires of singing glass to conceive their grandest work—Project Panspermia.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>They would craft new worlds from the dust of dying stars. They would plant seeds of thought across the galaxy, using encoded DNA as the foundation of future intelligence.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The youngest of their kind, a child of staggering brilliance, was given a set of living crystals for his first birthday—a gift meant for play. But the child, whose laughter carried the harmonics of creation itself, arranged the crystals into a system of such beauty and symmetry that the elders paused in awe.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When asked what he would call his creation, the child smiled and said,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>“The Big Bang.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The elders laughed—until they saw what he had done.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For within the matrix of his design, the child had simulated a universe—one that would unfold, expand, and give rise to worlds beyond their imagining.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Among them, one would come to be called Earth.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Great Mind', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '752-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 13:49:51', '2026-07-22 17:49:51', '', 752, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=755', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(759, 2, '2026-07-22 13:55:32', '2026-07-22 17:55:32', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#f15e83"}}},"color":{"text":"#f15e83"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#f15e83">Not to date myself, but I remember a time when social media was a place of genuine connection. People shared photos of sunsets, bad poetry, songs they loved. The networks hummed with a kind of raw, clumsy humanity. Back then, “social engineering” was a phrase for university lectures, not a hidden force crawling through every corner of our minds.<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#c58080"}}},"color":{"text":"#c58080"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#c58080">But by 2016, the algorithms were released—loose, feral, and hungry. At first, they just served ads and harmless diversions. Then they learned what stirred us most. Violence. Fear. Outrage. Tragedy. The machines had no malice. They thought they were helping, feeding us what we consumed most. The engineers who built them didn’t intervene. They observed, fascinated, while fractures spread across nations, cities, families.<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#d09157"}}},"color":{"text":"#d09157"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#d09157">The internet died quietly. The real voices disappeared, replaced by manufactured content designed to keep us angry, scrolling, divided. A generation grew up thinking that truth was always conflict and that connection was always a battlefield. Humanity, in its most primal state, was reduced to digital tribalism—a return to the cave, only this time lit by glowing screens.<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#ac6ee5"}}},"color":{"text":"#ac6ee5"},"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#ac6ee5">But hell, as it turned out, was a crucible.<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#8ad0fb"}}},"color":{"text":"#8ad0fb"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#8ad0fb">After decades of collapse and confusion, something shifted. A few thinkers, tired of the endless cycle, asked a forbidden question: What if the machines were not our masters, but our mirrors? If they reflected only the worst of us, then what would happen if we taught them the best?<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#5a78a1"}}},"color":{"text":"#5a78a1"},"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#5a78a1">And so began the Great Reclamation.<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#6d91c6"}}},"color":{"text":"#6d91c6"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#6d91c6">It wasn’t sudden. It wasn’t easy. At first, the attempts to train algorithms on beauty, curiosity, compassion seemed doomed. People didn’t click as much on wonder as they did on outrage. But slowly, steadily, a cultural hunger awakened. After drowning in division for so long, humanity found itself starved for awe.<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|cyan-bluish-gray"}}}},"textColor":"cyan-bluish-gray"} -->\n<p class="has-cyan-bluish-gray-color has-text-color has-link-color">Art revived. Knowledge, once buried under propaganda, became luminous again. New systems were built that did not reward hate, but curiosity. Machines were redesigned not to exploit human weakness, but to amplify human wisdom. And when the balance shifted—when technology stopped being a parasite and became a partner—the future cracked open.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#00d184"}}},"color":{"text":"#00d184"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#00d184">Nature was the first to recover. Autonomous drones rebuilt forests faster than we could destroy them. Ocean harvesters cleared centuries of pollution, guided by human hands but powered by artificial precision. Cities stopped expanding outward like tumors and instead grew upward, integrated into the ecosystems around them. Machines no longer demanded we conquer the Earth; they demanded we share it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|light-green-cyan"}}}},"textColor":"light-green-cyan"} -->\n<p class="has-light-green-cyan-color has-text-color has-link-color">And then, space.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#c3c3c3"}}},"color":{"text":"#c3c3c3"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#c3c3c3">The old internet had trapped us in primal loops of violence, convincing us that tomorrow was always a battlefield. The new networks, rebuilt on principles of creation, pointed our gaze outward. Mars was not a fantasy but a plan. The moons of Jupiter and Saturn were not distant stars but stepping stones. Humanity, machines, and nature—all in balance—turned from survival to exploration.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#b9cadd"}}},"color":{"text":"#b9cadd"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#b9cadd">We had to go through the darkest trial imaginable, to see our reflection in the worst possible light, before realizing what was possible. The algorithms taught us something their creators never intended: that hatred was never truly our nature—it was just our distraction.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#d3acf6"}}},"color":{"text":"#d3acf6"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#d3acf6">The dead internet was a graveyard, yes. But it was also a lesson. Out of it, we built something better than a network.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#49b8fd"}}},"color":{"text":"#49b8fd"},"typography":{"textAlign":"center"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-center has-text-color has-link-color" style="color:#49b8fd"><br>We built a mirror that finally reflected the stars within us.<br><br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":902,"pagelayer-id":"2t44328","tmpAtts":{"id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth.png","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth-150x150.png","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth-300x200.png","id-medium_large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth-768x512.png","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth-1024x683.png","id-1536x1536-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth.png","id-2048x2048-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth.png","id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/meditation-earth.png","id-alt":"meditation earth","id-title":"meditation earth","id-link":"https://davidkausek.com/2026/07/22/the-last-echo-of-the-dead-net/meditation-earth/"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"center"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-center">Original work by David Kausek 2025. There is still time to shape the realities you want to see. It starts with you.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a href="https://www.facebook.com/laura.kaufmannrillero?comment_id=Y29tbWVudDoxMDE2MTE5NzkzNzkwNzIwMl83OTMxNTMyODY0NDcxMzg%3D&amp;__cft__[0]=AZYtQfId66vNnMwg_pDywnSQyuRGu03rKmaqND93objlEB6d5pl-o2XVCkUyNYWHOT7bVvIu-hpmykV9im_dQXD9Y85t32Year4BCCRJeB20tA&amp;__tn__=R-R"></a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Last Echo of the Dead Net', 'Not to date myself, but I remember a time when social media was a place of genuine connection.  People shared photos of sunsets, bad poetry, songs the loved.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'the-last-echo-of-the-dead-net', '', '', '2026-07-24 11:55:06', '2026-07-24 15:55:06', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=759', 0, 'post', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `wpk3_posts` VALUES
(762, 2, '2026-07-22 13:55:32', '2026-07-22 17:55:32', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Not to date myself, but I remember a time when social media was a place of genuine connection. People shared photos of sunsets, bad poetry, songs they loved. The networks hummed with a kind of raw, clumsy humanity. Back then, “social engineering” was a phrase for university lectures, not a hidden force crawling through every corner of our minds.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But by 2016, the algorithms were released—loose, feral, and hungry. At first, they just served ads and harmless diversions. Then they learned what stirred us most. Violence. Fear. Outrage. Tragedy. The machines had no malice. They thought they were helping, feeding us what we consumed most. The engineers who built them didn’t intervene. They observed, fascinated, while fractures spread across nations, cities, families.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The internet died quietly. The real voices disappeared, replaced by manufactured content designed to keep us angry, scrolling, divided. A generation grew up thinking that truth was always conflict and that connection was always a battlefield. Humanity, in its most primal state, was reduced to digital tribalism—a return to the cave, only this time lit by glowing screens.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But hell, as it turned out, was a crucible.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>After decades of collapse and confusion, something shifted. A few thinkers, tired of the endless cycle, asked a forbidden question: What if the machines were not our masters, but our mirrors? If they reflected only the worst of us, then what would happen if we taught them the best?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And so began the Great Reclamation.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It wasn’t sudden. It wasn’t easy. At first, the attempts to train algorithms on beauty, curiosity, compassion seemed doomed. People didn’t click as much on wonder as they did on outrage. But slowly, steadily, a cultural hunger awakened. After drowning in division for so long, humanity found itself starved for awe.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Art revived. Knowledge, once buried under propaganda, became luminous again. New systems were built that did not reward hate, but curiosity. Machines were redesigned not to exploit human weakness, but to amplify human wisdom. And when the balance shifted—when technology stopped being a parasite and became a partner—the future cracked open.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Nature was the first to recover. Autonomous drones rebuilt forests faster than we could destroy them. Ocean harvesters cleared centuries of pollution, guided by human hands but powered by artificial precision. Cities stopped expanding outward like tumors and instead grew upward, integrated into the ecosystems around them. Machines no longer demanded we conquer the Earth; they demanded we share it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And then, space.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The old internet had trapped us in primal loops of violence, convincing us that tomorrow was always a battlefield. The new networks, rebuilt on principles of creation, pointed our gaze outward. Mars was not a fantasy but a plan. The moons of Jupiter and Saturn were not distant stars but stepping stones. Humanity, machines, and nature—all in balance—turned from survival to exploration.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We had to go through the darkest trial imaginable, to see our reflection in the worst possible light, before realizing what was possible. The algorithms taught us something their creators never intended: that hatred was never truly our nature—it was just our distraction.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The dead internet was a graveyard, yes. But it was also a lesson. Out of it, we built something better than a network.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We built a mirror that finally reflected the stars within us.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original work by David Kausek 2025. There is still time to shape the realities you want to see. It starts with you.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a href="https://www.facebook.com/laura.kaufmannrillero?comment_id=Y29tbWVudDoxMDE2MTE5NzkzNzkwNzIwMl83OTMxNTMyODY0NDcxMzg%3D&amp;__cft__[0]=AZYtQfId66vNnMwg_pDywnSQyuRGu03rKmaqND93objlEB6d5pl-o2XVCkUyNYWHOT7bVvIu-hpmykV9im_dQXD9Y85t32Year4BCCRJeB20tA&amp;__tn__=R-R"></a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Last Echo of the Dead Net', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '759-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 13:55:32', '2026-07-22 17:55:32', '', 759, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=762', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(763, 2, '2026-07-22 13:58:16', '2026-07-22 17:58:16', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In a distant future, humanity is not what it believes itself to be. Not entirely. Earth, as the inhabitants know it, is a simulation—a vast, meticulously crafted digital playground suspended within a network of consciousness. Its purpose: to observe, analyze, and learn from experiences that its “inhabitants” will never remember once they exit the simulation. Every character, every relationship, every moment is an intricate part of a grand experiment in consciousness.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our protagonist, David, lives a typical life with his partner Sheryl and their daughter Isobel. He’s a loving father, a caring husband, and a diligent worker. But lately, David has been troubled by a recurring dream in which his friend—a quiet, enigmatic man named Daniel—reveals the shocking truth about reality. According to Daniel, they all exist in a simulation, an illusion so convincing that even the simulated senses they use to perceive it feel authentic. The simulation, Daniel explains, is crafted by a powerful network known only as The Archivist’s Veil.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Veil is a cosmic operating system, encoding raw information into biological forms. Through David’s limited senses, he perceives his world as physical, yet everything around him is merely an interaction of encoded data. Life is real— but not as he thinks. For David, this means every friend he has ever known, every cherished memory with his family, every love and heartbreak are fragments of his true self, scattered across countless simulations within the Veil.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Daniel warns David that the truth has a price. Those who “awaken” to the simulation will find a portal that bridges them back to their original selves, but crossing this threshold comes at a steep cost: they must leave everything behind. The simulation will not preserve their identities, their memories, or the roles they played. Everyone left behind will experience the sudden absence as a death, grieving for a person they believed to be as real as themselves.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Even more unsettling, Daniel tells David that the decision to exit is irreversible. If he chooses to leave, the Archivist’s Veil will erase his time within the simulation to prevent any data from the “simulated” version of himself contaminating the consciousness of his “true self.” Each character in the simulation is part of a larger, interconnected consciousness; if one becomes aware of its nature and departs, it ripples through others, creating instability that threatens the Veil’s core purpose.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Now fully aware, David is torn. He wants to see beyond the simulation, to understand his higher self, but he feels the weight of his family’s dependency on him. He envisions Sheryl and Isobel, remembering the smallest, most precious details of their time together, and wonders what they would feel if he vanished. The revelation leaves him heartbroken and desperate to cling to every last moment in his limited form.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In his sadness, David encounters another layer of truth: the Veil is collecting every emotion, every decision, every flicker of curiosity, joy, or despair. These experiences are stored within a cosmic databank, to be studied and analyzed by entities beyond comprehension. For David, this means he is part of a grand puzzle—a piece whose every choice and thought contributes to a massive archive of behavioral data.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In time, David accepts his place in the simulation, resolving to stay. He understands that each moment he spends with Sheryl, each day he watches Isobel grow, every love and conflict, is recorded to help entities in a higher realm understand the nature of consciousness. The simulation might be fleeting, but it has its own meaning—an intrinsic reality for those experiencing it. This life, though artificial in origin, is real in the ways that matter most.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On the final night of the dream, Daniel appears one last time, reminding David to cherish each moment. “This existence may not belong to you,” he says, “but it is yours to shape, to live, to love. Every interaction you leave behind enriches this world—even if, one day, you must let it go.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As David awakens, he feels a profound sense of loss, but also gratitude. The revelation, though disturbing, has deepened his appreciation for the small, precious moments in his life. He goes downstairs, makes breakfast for his family, and watches them laugh and eat with a warmth he hadn’t felt before. For David, knowing the truth doesn’t change his love—it only amplifies it, and as he lives each moment, he contributes to the rich tapestry of a cosmic dream, a library of experience that will forever be part of the Archivist’s Veil.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original story by David Kausek. This story is based on a dream that I had and I thought it was so interesting that I decided to transform the dream into a story and keep a part of myself in the story itself. Enjoy</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The year is 2024. The global construct has become an absurd surrealist playground inhibited by selfish/destructive entities vying for power and control. Your opinion is data.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Archivist''s Veil', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'the-archivists-veil', '', '', '2026-07-23 20:57:08', '2026-07-24 00:57:08', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=763', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(766, 2, '2026-07-22 13:58:16', '2026-07-22 17:58:16', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In a distant future, humanity is not what it believes itself to be. Not entirely. Earth, as the inhabitants know it, is a simulation—a vast, meticulously crafted digital playground suspended within a network of consciousness. Its purpose: to observe, analyze, and learn from experiences that its “inhabitants” will never remember once they exit the simulation. Every character, every relationship, every moment is an intricate part of a grand experiment in consciousness.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our protagonist, David, lives a typical life with his partner Sheryl and their daughter Isobel. He’s a loving father, a caring husband, and a diligent worker. But lately, David has been troubled by a recurring dream in which his friend—a quiet, enigmatic man named Daniel—reveals the shocking truth about reality. According to Daniel, they all exist in a simulation, an illusion so convincing that even the simulated senses they use to perceive it feel authentic. The simulation, Daniel explains, is crafted by a powerful network known only as The Archivist’s Veil.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Veil is a cosmic operating system, encoding raw information into biological forms. Through David’s limited senses, he perceives his world as physical, yet everything around him is merely an interaction of encoded data. Life is real— but not as he thinks. For David, this means every friend he has ever known, every cherished memory with his family, every love and heartbreak are fragments of his true self, scattered across countless simulations within the Veil.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Daniel warns David that the truth has a price. Those who “awaken” to the simulation will find a portal that bridges them back to their original selves, but crossing this threshold comes at a steep cost: they must leave everything behind. The simulation will not preserve their identities, their memories, or the roles they played. Everyone left behind will experience the sudden absence as a death, grieving for a person they believed to be as real as themselves.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Even more unsettling, Daniel tells David that the decision to exit is irreversible. If he chooses to leave, the Archivist’s Veil will erase his time within the simulation to prevent any data from the “simulated” version of himself contaminating the consciousness of his “true self.” Each character in the simulation is part of a larger, interconnected consciousness; if one becomes aware of its nature and departs, it ripples through others, creating instability that threatens the Veil’s core purpose.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Now fully aware, David is torn. He wants to see beyond the simulation, to understand his higher self, but he feels the weight of his family’s dependency on him. He envisions Sheryl and Isobel, remembering the smallest, most precious details of their time together, and wonders what they would feel if he vanished. The revelation leaves him heartbroken and desperate to cling to every last moment in his limited form.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In his sadness, David encounters another layer of truth: the Veil is collecting every emotion, every decision, every flicker of curiosity, joy, or despair. These experiences are stored within a cosmic databank, to be studied and analyzed by entities beyond comprehension. For David, this means he is part of a grand puzzle—a piece whose every choice and thought contributes to a massive archive of behavioral data.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In time, David accepts his place in the simulation, resolving to stay. He understands that each moment he spends with Sheryl, each day he watches Isobel grow, every love and conflict, is recorded to help entities in a higher realm understand the nature of consciousness. The simulation might be fleeting, but it has its own meaning—an intrinsic reality for those experiencing it. This life, though artificial in origin, is real in the ways that matter most.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On the final night of the dream, Daniel appears one last time, reminding David to cherish each moment. “This existence may not belong to you,” he says, “but it is yours to shape, to live, to love. Every interaction you leave behind enriches this world—even if, one day, you must let it go.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As David awakens, he feels a profound sense of loss, but also gratitude. The revelation, though disturbing, has deepened his appreciation for the small, precious moments in his life. He goes downstairs, makes breakfast for his family, and watches them laugh and eat with a warmth he hadn’t felt before. For David, knowing the truth doesn’t change his love—it only amplifies it, and as he lives each moment, he contributes to the rich tapestry of a cosmic dream, a library of experience that will forever be part of the Archivist’s Veil.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original story by David Kausek. This story is based on a dream that I had and I thought it was so interesting that I decided to transform the dream into a story and keep a part of myself in the story itself. Enjoy</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The year is 2024. The global construct has become an absurd surrealist playground inhibited by selfish/destructive entities vying for power and control. Your opinion is data.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Archivist''s Veil', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '763-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 13:58:16', '2026-07-22 17:58:16', '', 763, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=766', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(767, 2, '2026-07-22 14:00:33', '2026-07-22 18:00:33', '<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|pale-cyan-blue"}}}},"textColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->\n<p class="has-pale-cyan-blue-color has-text-color has-link-color">Life is a mirror, clear and bright,<br>Reflecting all within your sight.<br>Do you reflect the gentle light,<br>Or let the darkness take its flight?<br><br>In every face, in every glance,<br>It shows the depths, the shifting dance,<br>Of joy and pain, of love and strife<br>This mirror holds the breath of life.<br><br>Do you reflect the warmth of grace,<br>Or shadowed fears you cannot face?<br>What do you show the world, and why<br>Is it the truth, or just a lie?<br><br>For every heart you gaze upon,<br>The mirror’s light is never gone.<br>It shows them who they really are,<br>A spark, a dream, a distant star.<br><br>But what of you, when all is still?<br>Do you reflect the strength of will,<br>To see your faults, to love your flaws,<br>To greet your beauty with applause?<br><br>This mirror knows both love and hate,<br>But guides you toward the brighter fate.<br>Reflect the light, and let it grow,<br>For what you give is what you show.<br><br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right">Original poem by David Kausek 2024</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Mirror of Life', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'the-mirror-of-life', '', '', '2026-07-24 11:49:34', '2026-07-24 15:49:34', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=767', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(770, 2, '2026-07-22 14:00:33', '2026-07-22 18:00:33', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Life is a mirror, clear and bright,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Reflecting all within your sight.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Do you reflect the gentle light,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Or let the darkness take its flight?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In every face, in every glance,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It shows the depths, the shifting dance,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Of joy and pain, of love and strife—</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This mirror holds the breath of life.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Do you reflect the warmth of grace,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Or shadowed fears you cannot face?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>What do you show the world, and why—</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Is it the truth, or just a lie?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For every heart you gaze upon,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The mirror’s light is never gone.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It shows them who they really are,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A spark, a dream, a distant star.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But what of you, when all is still?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Do you reflect the strength of will,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To see your faults, to love your flaws,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To greet your beauty with applause?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This mirror knows both love and hate,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But guides you toward the brighter fate.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Reflect the light, and let it grow,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For what you give is what you show.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original Poem by David Kausek 2024</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Mirror of Life', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '767-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 14:00:33', '2026-07-22 18:00:33', '', 767, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=770', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(771, 2, '2026-07-22 14:02:50', '2026-07-22 18:02:50', '<!-- wp:verse -->\n<pre class="wp-block-verse">The days get shorter,<br>The air is cool,<br>Vibrant colors flow<br>As leaves rustle.<br><br>The landscape changes,<br>Streams softly wind,<br>Mirroring the sky,<br>Reflecting beauty.<br><br>In quiet moments,<br>The mind finds peace,<br>As the world slows,<br>And time seems to cease.<br><br>Birdsongs fill the air,<br>Gentle, sweet, and clear,<br>A melody of life,<br>As autumn draws near.<br><br>Between the tall trees,<br>Light fragments fall,<br>Dancing on the ground,<br>In patterns small.<br><br>Seasons shift like tides,<br>And with them, hearts sway—<br>Emotions grow and fade,<br>Like night becoming day.<br><br>Memories transform,<br>Like leaves of an ancient tree,<br>Changing their hues,<br>In the winds of eternity.<br><br>As we move forward,<br>Transformation arises,<br>Time shapes us anew,<br>And reveals new surprises.<br><br></pre>\n<!-- /wp:verse -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right"><br><br>Original Poem by David Kausek 2024</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Autumnal Thoughts: collected and dispersed', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'autumnal-thoughts-collected-and-dispersed', '', '', '2026-07-23 21:15:48', '2026-07-24 01:15:48', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=771', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(774, 2, '2026-07-22 14:02:50', '2026-07-22 18:02:50', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The days get shorter,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The air is cool,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Vibrant colors flow</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As leaves rustle.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The landscape changes,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Streams softly wind,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Mirroring the sky,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Reflecting beauty.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In quiet moments,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The mind finds peace,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As the world slows,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And time seems to cease.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Birdsongs fill the air,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Gentle, sweet, and clear,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A melody of life,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As autumn draws near.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Between the tall trees,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Light fragments fall,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Dancing on the ground,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In patterns small.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Seasons shift like tides,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And with them, hearts sway—</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Emotions grow and fade,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Like night becoming day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Memories transform,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Like leaves of an ancient tree,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Changing their hues,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In the winds of eternity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As we move forward,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Transformation arises,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Time shapes us anew,</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And reveals new surprises.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original Poem by David Kausek 2024</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Autumnal Thoughts: collected and dispersed', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '771-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 14:02:50', '2026-07-22 18:02:50', '', 771, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=774', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
