h -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br><br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Desert Flower''s Darkness', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '834-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-22 17:34:05', '2026-07-22 21:34:05', '', 834, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=842', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(843, 2, '2026-07-23 14:02:55', '2026-07-23 18:02:55', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Amidst the sandy dunes and starry night.<br>There lies a flower amidst the vastness of nothing.<br>Its petals soft and delicate, yet strong.<br>As it blooms in the desert without witness.<br><br>In the darkness, it''s a sight to behold.<br>Its beauty shimmers like precious gold.<br>As the winds howl and the sands shift.<br>The flower stands firm, a desert gift.<br><br>Its color vibrant, like a fire''s flame.<br>A symbol of hope in a land so tame.<br>For in the emptiness of the arid plain.<br>This flower''s resilience is not in vain.<br><br>It survives in a place where life is rare.<br>A testament to the power of nature''s flair.<br>In the stillness of the moonlit night.<br>The desert flower shines so bright.<br><br>Oh, desert flower, you are a wonder.<br>A treasure in a land torn asunder.<br>In the darkness, you bring us light.<br>A symbol of hope, in the plight.<br><br>We live in a world of division.<br>Forgottten love exchanged for hatred.<br>A grab bag of data in isolation.<br>You are nothing but an accumulation of data.<br>Extrapolate/buy/sell/human simian.<br><br>Dehumanizing the present moment!<br><br>Your life is suffocated by false realities!<br>“Fear that which you do not comprehend!!!”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Child</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Night</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Light</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Illuminating this moment.<br><br>Embraced by the statues quo.<br>Cash out!<br>Sell out!!<br>Upload!!!<br><br>Be the “unoriginal being of fear!"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Be....</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>CONTROLLED!!!!!!!!!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br>Original poem by David Kausek 2023</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Desert Flower''s Darkness', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '834-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:02:55', '2026-07-23 18:02:55', '', 834, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=843', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(845, 2, '2026-07-23 14:06:13', '2026-07-23 18:06:13', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Life is a mirror, clear and bright,<br>Reflecting all within your sight.<br>Do you reflect the gentle light,<br>Or let the darkness take its flight?<br><br>In every face, in every glance,<br>It shows the depths, the shifting dance,<br>Of joy and pain, of love and strife<br>This mirror holds the breath of life.<br><br>Do you reflect the warmth of grace,<br>Or shadowed fears you cannot face?<br>What do you show the world, and why<br>Is it the truth, or just a lie?<br><br>For every heart you gaze upon,<br>The mirror’s light is never gone.<br>It shows them who they really are,<br>A spark, a dream, a distant star.<br><br>But what of you, when all is still?<br>Do you reflect the strength of will,<br>To see your faults, to love your flaws,<br>To greet your beauty with applause?<br><br>This mirror knows both love and hate,<br>But guides you toward the brighter fate.<br>Reflect the light, and let it grow,<br>For what you give is what you show.<br><br>Original Poem by David Kausek 2024</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Mirror of Life', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '767-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:06:13', '2026-07-23 18:06:13', '', 767, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=845', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(846, 2, '2026-07-23 14:06:43', '2026-07-23 18:06:43', '<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|pale-cyan-blue"}}}},"textColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->\n<p class="has-pale-cyan-blue-color has-text-color has-link-color">Life is a mirror, clear and bright,<br>Reflecting all within your sight.<br>Do you reflect the gentle light,<br>Or let the darkness take its flight?<br><br>In every face, in every glance,<br>It shows the depths, the shifting dance,<br>Of joy and pain, of love and strife<br>This mirror holds the breath of life.<br><br>Do you reflect the warmth of grace,<br>Or shadowed fears you cannot face?<br>What do you show the world, and why<br>Is it the truth, or just a lie?<br><br>For every heart you gaze upon,<br>The mirror’s light is never gone.<br>It shows them who they really are,<br>A spark, a dream, a distant star.<br><br>But what of you, when all is still?<br>Do you reflect the strength of will,<br>To see your faults, to love your flaws,<br>To greet your beauty with applause?<br><br>This mirror knows both love and hate,<br>But guides you toward the brighter fate.<br>Reflect the light, and let it grow,<br>For what you give is what you show.<br><br>Original Poem by David Kausek 2024</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Mirror of Life', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '767-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:06:43', '2026-07-23 18:06:43', '', 767, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=846', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(848, 2, '2026-07-23 14:08:38', '2026-07-23 18:08:38', '<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|pale-cyan-blue"}}}},"textColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->\n<p class="has-pale-cyan-blue-color has-text-color has-link-color">Amidst the sandy dunes and starry night.<br>There lies a flower amidst the vastness of nothing.<br>Its petals soft and delicate, yet strong.<br>As it blooms in the desert without witness.<br><br>In the darkness, it''s a sight to behold.<br>Its beauty shimmers like precious gold.<br>As the winds howl and the sands shift.<br>The flower stands firm, a desert gift.<br><br>Its color vibrant, like a fire''s flame.<br>A symbol of hope in a land so tame.<br>For in the emptiness of the arid plain.<br>This flower''s resilience is not in vain.<br><br>It survives in a place where life is rare.<br>A testament to the power of nature''s flair.<br>In the stillness of the moonlit night.<br>The desert flower shines so bright.<br><br>Oh, desert flower, you are a wonder.<br>A treasure in a land torn asunder.<br>In the darkness, you bring us light.<br>A symbol of hope, in the plight.<br><br>We live in a world of division.<br>Forgottten love exchanged for hatred.<br>A grab bag of data in isolation.<br>You are nothing but an accumulation of data.<br>Extrapolate/buy/sell/human simian.<br><br>Dehumanizing the present moment!<br><br>Your life is suffocated by false realities!<br>“Fear that which you do not comprehend!!!”<br><br>Child<br>Night<br>Light<br><br>Illuminating this moment.<br><br>Embraced by the statues quo.<br>Cash out!<br>Sell out!!<br>Upload!!!<br><br>Be the “unoriginal being of fear!"<br>Be....<br>CONTROLLED!!!!!!!!!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br>Original poem by David Kausek 2023</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Desert Flower''s Darkness', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '834-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:08:38', '2026-07-23 18:08:38', '', 834, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=848', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(849, 2, '2026-07-23 14:09:08', '2026-07-23 18:09:08', '<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|pale-cyan-blue"}}}},"textColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->\n<p class="has-pale-cyan-blue-color has-text-color has-link-color">Born among a digital paradigm shift<br>There lives a child with curious eyes<br>A spirit full of love and surprise<br><br>Her smile like the rising sun<br>A golden glow upon the horizon<br>Illuminates the Earth<br><br>Her eyes like diamonds glimmering with the ocean<br>Filling the world with vibrant colors<br>An artist with an effortless brush<br><br>Her eyes like diamonds glimmering with the ocean <br>Filling the world with vibrant colors <br>An artist with an effortless brush<br><br>Her laugh sings through the valleys of joy<br>Reminding us of the moment of our own birth<br>The wonders of life ever-present in distant memories<br><br>Her skin as sweet as the color of honey<br><br>This rainbow child, a life <br>Sings the song of cosmic angels <br>Her melody reminding us to look beyond the tragedy of death <br>And all those dreams that could have been<br><br>For all the unborn souls who faded too soon…<br><br>A moment of silence….<br><br>Those “little beans” that brought great joy <br>Before dying like the embers of a fire extinguished by violent rain <br>Bringing tears that flowed from the mountains <br>Washing away the pain and grief <br>A silent suffering shared by many <br>A taboo to speak the truth<br><br>With resonant sounds <br>The words sung with meaning <br>Reminds us of what it means to be human<br><br>This beautiful rainbow child shines bright against the darkest of skies <br>In a world of hope and a world of lies <br>Her majestic smile has the power to melt the ice of the coldest adult hearts<br><br>This child looks up at the fresh blue sky <br>Not knowing the cycles before her <br>All is full of wonder and curiosity <br>A reflection of our innermost being<br><br>With clarity <br>A beam of light <br>Parts the fog of modern distortions<br><br>The child can be heard across the land <br>Echoing the potentialities of what “can become” <br>The future grasped by little hands <br>So warm and loving <br>As fragile as a falling snowflake <br>Blanketing the forest filled with birds<br><br>This infant An ember in our hearts <br>Gazes upon the world with wonder and delight <br>Her smile is such an amazing sight <br>A divine beauty beyond words <br>Fills our mouth with silence <br>There are no words to express this feeling<br><br>We walk a path altered by new decisions <br>A journey traveled by our ancestors<br><br>Angelic spirits of light <br>Caress the faces of innocent beings<br><br>A fragrant wind <br>A lotus unfolds on the surface of a still lake <br>The most ancient mirror<br><br>A message in a bottle <br>Drifting towards us with magnetic force <br>What words were they trying to form? <br>A vibration of the soul <br>A gift from beyond<br><br>This parallel reality <br>Full of dimension <br>Time And space<br><br>We gaze upon the clear blue skies <br>With an obscure reminder of the most obscene <br>The most ancient cycles.. <br>All that lives must die <br>(Rebirth)<br><br>The sun shown bright <br>A moon circling the sphere<br><br>This cosmic song of the universe cannot be recorded<br><br>Only experienced directly <br>Through the subtle lens of observation<br><br>The curiosity of the mind <br>Reflects the truth of our being<br><br>The child shines bright <br>With tears of joy and delight<br><br>With the purity of heart, <br>Her voice can be heard <br>A landscape <br>A canvas <br>A child of art<br><br>Isobel Anaya <br>Daddy loves you forever and always <br>An eternal flame<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>An original poem by David Kausek.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'This curious child gazes skyward', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '818-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:09:08', '2026-07-23 18:09:08', '', 818, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=849', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(851, 2, '2026-07-23 14:12:23', '2026-07-23 18:12:23', '<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|pale-cyan-blue"}}}},"textColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->\n<p class="has-pale-cyan-blue-color has-text-color has-link-color">He sees the world through infinite perspectives.<br><br>A product of mind.<br>A lover of nature and computation.<br><br>Art is the expression of his magic.<br>His emotions are connected to his soul: abstractions induced by humanity’s reflections.<br>A modern day ancient being.<br><br>His actions are guided by intuition.<br>A dreamer who travels the universe within his mind.<br>The essence of freedom confined to body: a product of our time.<br><br>He presses his pallete towards his face and examines the pigments abstracted from Earth: a portal to another world.<br>So many hues and tones refracting light: such beauty surrounding space.<br><br>Each color pulsing with energy.<br>The abstraction of song embedded in paint: encoding meaning.<br>The sacred studio: a portal to another world.<br><br>Digital beings<br>Digital avatars<br>Digital daydreams</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|pale-cyan-blue"}}}},"textColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->\n<p class="has-pale-cyan-blue-color has-text-color has-link-color">Filling the void of the unknown<br><br>Child of creation.<br>Go forth and be free.<br>Let the world see its beauty!!!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original poem by David Kausek 2023</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'CHILD OF ART: birth of creation', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '813-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:12:23', '2026-07-23 18:12:23', '', 813, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=851', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(853, 2, '2026-07-23 14:16:26', '2026-07-23 18:16:26', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Hermit of Huntingville lived in a pivotal moment of change.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>     He was an interesting man who studied ancient manuscripts and society to try to find the true essence of humanity.<br>He was fascinated by the various ways human beings developed their own hierarchies based on their understanding of reality and he was fascinated by the ways human beings created religions to describe the spiritual dimensions of their minds.<br><br>     Terrence was the type of hermit who “did not speak as much as he observed” and he listened with his sharp mind that was scientifically advanced. He had a photographic memory and could replicate anything that he saw after seeing it once.<br><br>     As a child, Terrence was ostracized for not conforming to the social norms of his surroundings, but he did not really care because he was aware of the vast multitudes of societies and other ways of living that were running parallel to his reality. Terrence knew there were billions of peoples walking the Earth viewing the world in an almost infinite diversity of languages and customs and he became interested in the societies that carried on traditional ways of living for thousands of years.<br><br>     According to Terrence, all religions were social constructs developed through man and he viewed their stories of mythology with love and affection. He observed that societies throughout history had a knack for developing highly sophisticated explanations for everything from the origins of life to the realities that exist after one’s death and he was fascinated by the differences and similarities that each pocket of humanity had developed in their time and space.<br><br>     Terrence was not like most people. His true love was of nature and he studied butterflies in the Amazon. He studied literature and was obsessed with magical rites of people of tribal peoples and he deeply admired those who had a special connection to shamanism.<br><br>     During his travels through the forests, he experimented with the use of traditional plants and the ways they were utilized as medicines for tribal peoples. He approached indigenous people with interest and caution as he observed their ancient rites, rituals and customs, and he was lucky enough to be invited into their circles to witness directly what it was like to pay homage to their ancestors.<br><br>     Terrence traveled extensively around the world and studied the indigenous peoples while studying the various writings from his fellow scholars. Many of the tribesmen recognized Terrence as a child of nature but Terrence often laughed at that comparison and said he was just “a normal guy living an abnormal life.” One day while studying the connection between Siberian Natives and Native Americans of North America, Terrence fell asleep and had a very bizarre dream. In the dream, Terrence was visited by an intelligent spirit who said she was the great spirit known as the Mother Creator. In the dream, Terrence witnessed the rise and fall of civilizations and saw countless lifeforms come into existence and fade back into extinction. He witnessed countless variations of intelligence being birthed and removed from Earth and saw landscapes transform before his eyes. In this dream, the mother spirit told him that humanity was an experiment in intelligent awareness and that the sapiens were gifted with insights into higher forms of consciousness because they showed great potential. Terrence was terrified by this dream because he grew up thinking he was the highest form of intelligence that ever existed, but the Mother Spirit reminded him that his very existence was simply an experiment dealing with biological manifestations and their connection to consciousness. The Spirit lovingly told Terrence that his job was to create a tool more powerful than him and that his life was relatively insignificant when compared to the countless other lifeforms that were pushed back into extinction by the great Mother…. During a brief description of life, the Great Spirit laughed and said “I am your mother, I brought you into this world and I can take you out!”<br><br>     Upon waking from the dream, Terrence was shaken but not stirred. He was greeted by an elder tribesman that told him the Earth has been created and destroyed several times before and that the balance of life has always shifted from good to bad and back again. The tribesman told Terrence that his spirit was eternal but his experiences and body were only temporary constructs designed to give him a unique experience of being alive.<br>     <br>     When Terrence asked the tribesman about his dream, the tribesman laughed at him and said “All of life is but a dream. We are just living in a dream within a dream of the great Mother. And you are nothing but a child of nature.” Terrence felt very uncomfortable with what he had seen and witnessed in his dream and he told the tribesman to go fuck himself and went back home to go shop on Amazon and pretend like he was just an average Joe.<br><br>     Terrence was so upset that he legally changed his name to Jim and spent the rest of his years writing about the greatness of Roman civilization, warfare, butterflies and the death of countless Earth species that were dropping like flies. Jim spent several years self-publishing and congratulating himself on his miraculous achievements and he died a lonely man and was cremated. The local townsfolk didn’t really care much for Jim and they had his ashes scattered in their Wal-Mart parking lot so he could still be a part of the community and meet at the crossroads of their modern civilization.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>An original short story about an unoriginal man. (Story by David Kausek 2023)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Hermit of Huntingville', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '809-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:16:26', '2026-07-23 18:16:26', '', 809, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=853', 0, 'revision', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `wpk3_posts` VALUES
(856, 2, '2026-07-23 14:21:34', '2026-07-23 18:21:34', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Do dreams have dreams?<br>(Asked the sleeping child)<br><br>In the mind of an artist<br><br>The world becomes a language of symbols<br><br>Some ancient<br>Some modern<br>Some revealing<br>Some misleading<br><br>The world is a canvas<br>An expressive field of reciprocity<br><br>All things outside echo within<br>All things inside project outward<br><br>What does it mean to be human?<br><br>Emotions are states of consciousness<br>Biochemical currents within the brain<br>Conjuring a solid sense of now<br><br>The heart beats faster<br>The blood moves quicker<br>Cortisol levels rise<br><br>Perception is power<br>A frame assembled in the mind<br>A portrait shaped from concept<br><br>The artist breathes life into the inanimate<br>Words, notes, and pigments<br>Dreaming through experience<br><br>Truth lives within abstraction<br>The soul of the artist becomes a passage<br>Like a forest trail guiding perception<br><br>Each time the experiencer crosses the path<br>The scenery subtly alters<br>The trail bends almost unnoticed<br><br>The state of consciousness is a portal<br>A doorway into presence<br>An invitation into dreaming<br><br>Words are pigments of the mind<br>Spoken through the canvas of imagination<br>Fragments of understanding<br><br>The child awakens<br>A dream within a dream</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Original poetic sketch by David Kausek 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":678,"pagelayer-id":"p4s8615","tmpAtts":{"id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child.jpg","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-225x300.jpg","id-medium_large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-768x1024.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-768x1024.jpg","id-1536x1536-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child-1152x1536.jpg","id-2048x2048-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child.jpg","id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dreaming-child.jpg","id-alt":"dreaming child","id-title":"dreaming child","id-link":"https://davidkausek.com/dreaming-child/"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'do dreams have dreams?', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '738-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 14:21:34', '2026-07-23 18:21:34', '', 738, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=856', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
