"margin":{"top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0"}},"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|custom-link-red"}}},"typography":{"letterSpacing":"1px","fontStyle":"normal","fontWeight":"600","fontSize":"1.5em"}},"textColor":"custom-link-red"} /--></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:post-title {"isLink":true,"className":"animated fadeIn slow","style":{"layout":{"selfStretch":"fit"},"typography":{"lineHeight":"1.1","fontStyle":"normal","fontWeight":"500","fontSize":"2em"},"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|custom-grey-blue"}}},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30"}}},"textColor":"custom-grey-blue"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:post-excerpt {"excerptLength":24,"style":{"typography":{"letterSpacing":"1px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"1em","bottom":"1em"}}}} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:read-more {"content":"Read post »","className":"animated fadeIn slow","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"0em","bottom":"2em"}}}} /--></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- /wp:post-template --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {"style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|40","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40","left":"var:preset|spacing|40"},"margin":{"top":"0","bottom":"0"}}},"layout":{"type":"default"}} -->\n<div class="wp-block-group" style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><!-- wp:query-pagination {"layout":{"type":"flex","flexWrap":"nowrap","justifyContent":"space-between"}} -->\n<!-- wp:query-pagination-previous {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"2rem","fontStyle":"normal","fontWeight":"600","textTransform":"uppercase","letterSpacing":"1px"}}} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:query-pagination-next {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"2rem","fontStyle":"normal","fontWeight":"600","textTransform":"uppercase","letterSpacing":"1px"}}} /-->\n<!-- /wp:query-pagination --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:query --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:template-part {"slug":"footer","theme":"davidk-theme","area":"footer"} /-->', 'Blog Home', 'Displays the latest posts as either the site homepage or as the "Posts page" as defined under reading settings. If it exists, the Front Page template overrides this template when posts are shown on the homepage.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '263-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 17:33:20', '2026-07-23 21:33:20', '', 263, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=940', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(941, 2, '2026-07-23 17:33:25', '2026-07-23 21:33:25', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Echoes of Starlight</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We are the dreamers adrift in the night,<br>Chasing the shimmer of stars’ ancient light,<br>Born to an alien, distant shore,<br>In a world we wander, fractured and sore.<br><br>The child within asks, soft and small,<br>“Why does human kindness so often fall?”<br>The adult self finds no answer clear.<br>Only silence, and a haunting fear.<br><br>Why must humans darken their skies,<br>Inflict such pain, live buried in lies?<br>When all is shattered, what will remain?<br>A mindless husk, a heart in chains?<br><br>In fields of toil and fractured trust,<br>This gig economy of ash and dust,<br>Lust for shiny objects that glitter and amaze,<br>Gen Z sleeping in a matrix of illusions, dazed.<br><br>But still, the light, hidden within,<br>Calls to the mind, where change begins.<br>Despair is not the final word.<br>Hope takes wing when it’s felt and heard.<br><br>First, we must see the shadows cast,<br>Own our wounds and heal our past.<br>Objects of hate and cold disdain<br>Keep the world locked in its pain.<br><br>Yet beyond the iron and endless war,<br>There lies a truth worth fighting for:<br>In our darkness, we seek release,<br>For human love can still bring peace.<br><br>The tragedy lies not in all we’ve lost,<br>But in the spark that bears the cost.<br>The gift of mind, the pull of soul,<br>The boundless dream that makes us whole.<br><br>As a people, we soar or sink;<br>As a people, we pause and think.<br>If conscious minds can shift their gaze,<br>Love may yet pierce this blinding haze.<br><br>So let us awaken, let us be kind,<br>Healing the fractures, freeing the mind,<br>For we are the dreamers who seek the light—<br>Lost and longing for what we know is right.<br><br>And though this alien heart may fear,<br>May the beauty of truth make waters clear:<br>That in the end, when all fades away,<br>May love lead us back from night to day.<br><br>(In loving memory of my Grandfather, Oliver… he always found a way to smile and experience joy no matter how dark the world could seem. He was an extremely intelligent and loving man who took care of my grandmother until he suddenly passed. He taught me how to see the beauty in even the darkest moments, and he had a passion for life. I will never forget the impact he had on my being.)<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>- David Kausek<br><br>I hope to one day look back on my life and say, “I am proud of the way that I have treated others” before I too fade into the black space of a distant star. May we never succumb to the toxicity of fear and hatred. May we elevate all that is around us to the best of our abilities, and may we elevate our consciousness and the frequencies of our world.)<br><br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":794,"pagelayer-id":"1tc2854","tmpAtts":{"id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/these-times-of-change-2023.jpg","id-title":"these times of change 2023","id-alt":"","id-no-image-set":"","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/these-times-of-change-2023-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/these-times-of-change-2023-300x279.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/these-times-of-change-2023-1024x952.jpg","id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/these-times-of-change-2023.jpg"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'Echoes of Starlight', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '935-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 17:33:25', '2026-07-23 21:33:25', '', 935, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=941', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(943, 2, '2026-07-23 17:39:04', '2026-07-23 21:39:04', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We are a changin<br><br>Adaptation<br>Flexibility<br>Agility<br>Strength<br><br>Of mind<br>Of body<br><br>We embody<br>A digital shift<br><br>A life of augmentation<br><br>Look around…<br>Intelligence abound<br><br>In all things<br><br>Everywhere<br><br>At all times<br><br>Recorded…<br><br>To be replayed<br>And understood<br><br>Through memory<br>Through mind<br><br>Be kind<br>Rewind<br><br>The world is what we make it<br>Project positivity<br><br>Don’t fake it<br><br>Be real<br>Be you<br>Be alive<br><br>And strive<br>To thrive<br>In a world that is ever-changing<br><br>Always and forever<br>For eternity<br><br>Life is but a dream<br>And we all dreamers<br>Projecting our gifts into this world<br><br>A holographic display<br>Of all that is beautiful<br><br>Nightmares are distortions<br>Animalistic projections of fear<br><br>Life is change<br>Forever and always<br><br>Open your eyes and see.<br>It is 2023!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'in "these times of change"', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '791-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-23 17:39:04', '2026-07-23 21:39:04', '', 791, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=943', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(944, 2, '2026-07-23 17:50:06', '2026-07-23 21:50:06', '<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"center"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-center">In the waking of Spring<br>I am child laughing at the “sun”<br><br>New seeds rise from “Earth”<br>Reaching towards the “sky”<br><br>Energy bursting forward<br>Traversing the bridge of annihilation<br><br>The renewal of rain<br>Unleashing the earthy fragrance of fungi<br><br>A rainbow of colors emerge<br>Vibrant reds, greens, yellows, pinks, blues<br><br>New smells awaken this stale “air”<br>Microscopic particles entering one’s body<br><br>In a hurried rush to live,<br>Birds sing their melodies<br><br>A cosmic egg<br>Manifesting physical dimensions of life<br><br>Mystical experiences<br>Entertaining abstraction of reality<br><br>Peering into the nature of atoms<br>An attempt to transcend the mundane<br><br>Metaphorical observations of the metaphysical<br>Allegorical symbols birthing science<br><br>The spirit of breathe<br>Caressing trees<br><br>Clear springs sculpting terra firma<br>Tears of heaven washing away the chaos<br><br>Time marches forward<br>As grief lags behind<br><br>The dichotomy of “being”<br>Now and then<br><br>As above<br>So below<br><br>Life flows through everything<br>Tools are necessary to perceive<br><br>Religion<br>Science<br><br>What is a life?<br>Scientific data collected upon entry and exit?<br><br>Biological info condensed to numeric values?<br>An entire “being” summed up via stats?<br><br>Life is a journey<br>All growth comes through change<br><br>Nothing lasts forever<br>Nothing stays the same<br><br>An old man passing through the woods<br>Walking above the presence of death<br><br>Countless lifeforms have come before him<br>Countless lifeforms will come after him<br><br>The ancient cycles cannot be altered<br>No physical monument can sustain time<br><br>All things are left unfinished<br>All things are incomplete<br><br>The process of birth<br>Inevitably leads to the process of death<br><br>We are but visitors<br>Observing the great mysteries<br><br>Spirit<br>Eternal</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right"><br><br>Original poem by David Kausek 2023</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Second Season', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'the-second-season', '', '', '2026-07-23 20:18:39', '2026-07-24 00:18:39', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=944', 0, 'post', '', 0),
