and <br>Echoing the potentialities of what “can become” <br>The future grasped by little hands <br>So warm and loving <br>As fragile as a falling snowflake <br>Blanketing the forest filled with birds<br><br>This infant, an ember in our hearts, <br>Gazes upon the world with wonder and delight <br>Her smile is such an amazing sight <br>A divine beauty beyond words <br>Fills our mouth with silence <br>There are no words to express this feeling<br><br>We walk a path altered by new decisions <br>A journey traveled by our ancestors<br><br>Angelic spirits of light <br>Caress the faces of innocent beings<br><br>A fragrant wind <br>A lotus unfolds on the surface of a still lake <br>The most ancient mirror<br><br>A message in a bottle <br>Drifting towards us with magnetic force <br>What words were they trying to form? <br>A vibration of the soul <br>A gift from beyond<br><br>This parallel reality <br>Full of dimension <br>Time and space<br><br>We gaze upon the clear blue skies <br>With an obscure reminder of the most obscene <br>The most ancient cycles.. <br>All that lives must die <br>(Rebirth)<br><br>The sun shown bright <br>A moon circling the sphere<br><br>This cosmic song of the universe cannot be recorded<br><br>Only experienced directly <br>Through the subtle lens of observation<br><br>The curiosity of the mind <br>Reflects the truth of our being<br><br>The child shines bright <br>With tears of joy and delight<br><br>With the purity of heart, <br>Her voice can be heard </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|pale-cyan-blue"}}},"typography":{"textAlign":"center"}},"textColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-center has-pale-cyan-blue-color has-text-color has-link-color"><br>A landscape <br>A canvas <br>A child of art<br><br>Isobel Anaya <br>Daddy loves you forever and always <br>An eternal flame<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right"><br><br>Original poem by David Kausek</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'This curious child gazes skyward', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '818-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-24 13:27:18', '2026-07-24 17:27:18', '', 818, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=1130', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(1131, 2, '2026-07-24 13:30:55', '2026-07-24 17:30:55', '<!-- wp:verse {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"center"}}} -->\n<pre class="wp-block-verse has-text-align-center">Falling from the sky<br>With the grace of wind<br><br>A smile cannot pretend<br>Words like “love” and “friend”<br><br>An echo from the past<br>Haunting the streets of his childhood<br><br>Walking through dreams<br>From once upon a time<br><br>A beautiful pattern<br>Dancing in light and shadow<br><br>The interplay of complexity<br>Simplified by mind<br><br>Compassion warming the heart<br>From a cold blank space<br><br>Memories of love<br>Filling the void<br><br>Like water in a chalice<br>Releasing all malice<br><br>Forgiveness from fragile beings<br>Holding together, exterior strength<br><br>Like a healer purifying the land<br>He touches time with his hand<br><br>One cannot hold the intangible<br>Or grasp the meaning of infinity<br><br>Through complex processes<br>This poison must be dissolved<br><br>The clarity of water<br>Flowing through a peaceful stream<br><br>Symbolic sacrifices<br>Invoking the spirit of nature<br><br>Dynamic dimensions of time<br>Acting on perceptions internal<br><br>Knowledge of our ancestors<br>Guided by the eternal dreamer<br><br>Encoded information<br>Hidden within the mundane<br><br>In the flatness of a prairie<br>Where heaven touches the plains<br><br>One cannot lose contact with “human”<br>The essential self buried in distraction<br><br>Alchemical matter<br>A construct of the mind<br><br>Piercing the veil of Maya<br>A puzzle to be solved<br><br>The silence of a monk<br>Sacred is the vow<br><br>An image of the world<br>Transformed by the hands of an artist<br><br>The studio is his sanctuary<br>Holy acts of creation<br><br>Lifting the souls of man<br>Silence filling space<br><br>A counterweight to hatred and destruction<br>This hall of mirrors, society’s construction<br><br>A deep blue shadow<br>Wrapping around a face<br><br>A piece of the the soul<br>Captured like amber in oil<br><br>An open canvas<br>Expressing change<br><br>Like clarity in water<br>Filtered by action<br><br>Organic matter<br>Transferred into words<br><br>Enigmatic presence<br>Never waking from God’s dream<br><br></pre>\n<!-- /wp:verse -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right"><br><br>Original poem by David Kausek 2023</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', '"Glittering Gold"', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '962-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-24 13:30:55', '2026-07-24 17:30:55', '', 962, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=1131', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(1132, 1, '2026-07-24 13:39:47', '2026-07-24 17:39:47', '<!-- wp:cover {"url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/nature04-1024x768.jpg","id":211,"hasParallax":true,"dimRatio":80,"overlayColor":"custom-dark-gray","isUserOverlayColor":true,"minHeight":340,"contentPosition":"center center","sizeSlug":"large","className":"subpageHeader","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"left":"4vw","top":"8vh","right":"4vw","bottom":"4vh"}}},"layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->\n<div class="wp-block-cover has-parallax subpageHeader" style="padding-top:8vh;padding-right:4vw;padding-bottom:4vh;padding-left:4vw;min-height:340px"><div class="wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-211 size-large has-parallax" style="background-position:50% 50%;background-image:url(https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/nature04-1024x768.jpg)"></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-cover__background has-custom-dark-gray-background-color has-background-dim-80 has-background-dim"></span><div class="wp-block-cover__inner-container"><!-- wp:heading {"className":"animated fadeIn slow","style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|custom-link-red"}}}},"textColor":"custom-link-red"} -->\n<h2 class="wp-block-heading animated fadeIn slow has-custom-link-red-color has-text-color has-link-color">Heading</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"animated fadeIn slow","style":{"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"var:preset|color|white"}}},"typography":{"fontSize":"1.3em"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"0.8em"}}},"textColor":"white"} -->\n<p class="animated fadeIn slow has-white-color has-text-color has-link-color" style="padding-top:0.8em;font-size:1.3em">Lorem ipsum</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class="wp-block-buttons"><!-- wp:button {"backgroundColor":"custom-darker-gray","className":"animated fadeIn slow is-style-fill"} -->\n<div class="wp-block-button animated fadeIn slow is-style-fill"><a class="wp-block-button__link has-custom-darker-gray-background-color has-background wp-element-button">Button</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button -->\n\n<!-- wp:button {"backgroundColor":"custom-darker-gray","className":"animated fadeIn slow is-style-fill"} -->\n<div class="wp-block-button animated fadeIn slow is-style-fill"><a class="wp-block-button__link has-custom-darker-gray-background-color has-background wp-element-button">Button</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->', 'Hero', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'hero', '', '', '2026-08-01 12:26:19', '2026-08-01 16:26:19', '', 0, 'https://davidkausek.com/2026/07/24/hero/', 0, 'wp_block', '', 0),
(1134, 2, '2026-07-24 13:49:58', '2026-07-24 17:49:58', '<!-- wp:verse -->\n<pre class="wp-block-verse">The sacred cycle of life permeates all known things,<br>Reflecting an image of the divine.<br><br>From the first breath we take, to that moment our breath is extinguished,<br>We enter this ancient world anew.<br>With a perspective unlike any other,<br>We enter this world, pure and innocent,<br>With a heart full of love and wonderment, we learn to see the world according to our environment and the various things we are exposed to.<br><br>As time moves forward,<br>We repeat the process of humanity.<br><br>We grow and we learn, we stumble and fall.<br>We pick ourselves up and we stand tall.<br>We laugh and we cry, we love and we hate,<br>We experience joy and we experience all the intricacies of a vast emotional landscape, and, yes, sometimes we even suffer heartache.<br><br>The lessons we receive can be interpreted through a lens of clarity or a lens of distortion. <br>Nature is far more complex than the dichotomous perspectives we place upon it.<br>We are constantly trying to simplify, rationalize, codify and document our experiences (while our egos filter our realities).<br><br>Life is like looking out of a window,<br>You are inside the structure of body, but the mind peers through the glass as the windows of our soul collects information.<br><br>We touch, we feel, we hear, we smell, we analyze and we play.<br>We gather knowledge to shed light on new things and dispel the darkness of our collective ignorance.<br><br>Through it all, we are a part of this whole,<br>A symbiotic system of creation and destruction ruled by the laws of the Universe.<br><br>We are all floating through space on this “little blue dot” that has many names. <br>Some call it heaven, some call it hell, some call it Gaia and some call it spaceship Earth, but all of us call this planet home.<br><br>Gravity keeps us grounded but it also holds us down. <br>We learn the methods to overcome these limitations and we strive to push forward and explore new horizons.<br><br>The sun rises and sets according to our perspective on this spinning sphere of life, the seasons come and go,<br>And in the end, our matter returns to the earth below and there is always work left undone.<br><br>But our legacy lives on, in the lives we touched.<br>It lives through the laughter we shared,<br>In the memories we made, and in the love we expand outward in all directions.<br><br>The sacred cycle of life, is like a circle and each person is the center of that circle, expanding and contracting. <br>We chose to create and we chose to destroy, as we nourish the Yin and Yang of our beings.<br><br>Irregardless of the choices we make,<br>This planet continues to spin,<br>And we are all a part of it, from beginning to end.<br><br>Never forget that which is good, <br>Never let the darkness of space <br>Steal the light of your sun!<br><br>Carry on and lift as many as you can while you can.<br><br>Life is simple.<br>Life is complex.<br><br>We are just a fragment of the puzzle we call life. And the greatest mystery lies in our attempts to balance of all the forces within ourselves with the forces that flow through the entire cosmos.</pre>\n<!-- /wp:verse -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right">Original poem by David Kausek 2023</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":1119,"id-size":"large","pagelayer-id":"jwc9068","tmpAtts":{"id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses.jpg","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-225x300.jpg","id-medium_large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-768x1024.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-768x1024.jpg","id-1536x1536-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-1152x1536.jpg","id-2048x2048-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses.jpg","id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses.jpg","id-alt":"sunglasses","id-link":"https://davidkausek.com/2026/07/23/the-sacred-cycle/sunglasses/"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'The Sacred Cycle', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '975-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-24 13:49:58', '2026-07-24 17:49:58', '', 975, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=1134', 0, 'revision', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `wpk3_posts` VALUES
(1136, 2, '2026-07-24 13:53:30', '2026-07-24 17:53:30', '<!-- wp:verse -->\n<pre class="wp-block-verse">The sacred cycle of life permeates all known things,<br>Reflecting an image of the divine.<br><br>From the first breath we take, to that moment our breath is extinguished,<br>We enter this ancient world anew.<br>With a perspective unlike any other,<br>We enter this world, pure and innocent,<br>With a heart full of love and wonderment, we learn to see the world according to our environment and the various things we are exposed to.<br><br>As time moves forward,<br>We repeat the process of humanity.<br><br>We grow and we learn, we stumble and fall.<br>We pick ourselves up and we stand tall.<br>We laugh and we cry, we love and we hate,<br>We experience joy and we experience all the intricacies of a vast emotional landscape, and, yes, sometimes we even suffer heartache.<br><br>The lessons we receive can be interpreted through a lens of clarity or a lens of distortion. <br>Nature is far more complex than the dichotomous perspectives we place upon it.<br>We are constantly trying to simplify, rationalize, codify and document our experiences (while our egos filter our realities).<br><br>Life is like looking out of a window,<br>You are inside the structure of body, but the mind peers through the glass as the windows of our soul collects information.<br><br>We touch, we feel, we hear, we smell, we analyze and we play.<br>We gather knowledge to shed light on new things and dispel the darkness of our collective ignorance.<br><br>Through it all, we are a part of this whole,<br>A symbiotic system of creation and destruction ruled by the laws of the Universe.<br><br>We are all floating through space on this “little blue dot” that has many names. <br>Some call it heaven, some call it hell, some call it Gaia and some call it spaceship Earth, but all of us call this planet home.<br><br>Gravity keeps us grounded but it also holds us down. <br>We learn the methods to overcome these limitations and we strive to push forward and explore new horizons.<br><br>The sun rises and sets according to our perspective on this spinning sphere of life, the seasons come and go,<br>And in the end, our matter returns to the earth below and there is always work left undone.<br><br>But our legacy lives on, in the lives we touched.<br>It lives through the laughter we shared,<br>In the memories we made, and in the love we expand outward in all directions.<br><br>The sacred cycle of life, is like a circle and each person is the center of that circle, expanding and contracting. <br>We chose to create and we chose to destroy, as we nourish the Yin and Yang of our beings.<br><br>Irregardless of the choices we make,<br>This planet continues to spin,<br>And we are all a part of it, from beginning to end.<br><br>Never forget that which is good, <br>Never let the darkness of space <br>Steal the light of your sun!<br><br>Carry on and lift as many as you can while you can.<br><br>Life is simple.<br>Life is complex.<br><br>We are fragments of the puzzle known as life. <br>The greatest mystery is not control, but harmony—the work of balancing the forces inside us with the forces that shape the universe.</pre>\n<!-- /wp:verse -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"right"}}} -->\n<p class="has-text-align-right">Original poem by David Kausek 2023</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {"height":"3em"} -->\n<div style="height:3em" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:pagelayer/pl-image {"id":1119,"id-size":"large","pagelayer-id":"jwc9068","tmpAtts":{"id-full-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses.jpg","id-thumbnail-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-150x150.jpg","id-medium-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-225x300.jpg","id-medium_large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-768x1024.jpg","id-large-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-768x1024.jpg","id-1536x1536-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses-1152x1536.jpg","id-2048x2048-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses.jpg","id-url":"https://davidkausek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/sunglasses.jpg","id-alt":"sunglasses","id-link":"https://davidkausek.com/2026/07/23/the-sacred-cycle/sunglasses/"}} -->\n<p>Lorem Ipsum has been the industry''s standard dummy text ever since the 1500s.</p>\n<!-- /wp:pagelayer/pl-image -->', 'The Sacred Cycle', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '975-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-24 13:53:30', '2026-07-24 17:53:30', '', 975, 'https://davidkausek.com/?p=1136', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
